# Files whose job is to name identifiers that do not resolve.
#
# Check 6 asks that every identifier a change writes into a file exists on
# spec@main. A test of "refuse an unknown identifier" has to write one that does
# not, and a test of the next free number has to write ones past the ceiling —
# so reading these would have the gate refuse the change that teaches it to
# refuse, and the only way out would be fixtures built from real requirement
# numbers, which drift the moment the spec moves.
#
# `spec_check.py` and `test_spec_check.py` are skipped by the gate itself and are
# deliberately not repeated here: this list is for a repository's own fixtures,
# and a line that could be deleted without effect is a line nobody trusts.
#
# Exact paths only. Every one of these is printed on every run.
scripts/test_closing.py
scripts/test_goal_coverage.py
scripts/test_integrity.py
scripts/test_milestone.py
scripts/test_next_id.py
scripts/test_order.py
scripts/test_status_lint.py
